A “sports utility” vehicle was never supposed to be sporty. It was a way to pack up all your gear and your family, and go wherever you do your sports-related activity. You could take it off road, and nobody cared if the back seat got dirty. So, utilized for sports.

Of course, most SUVs are driven to the office or the grocery store, and have never been defiled by a dirty bicycle.  Mine is mainly a dog limo. Although they can get a little sporty, so maybe that counts?

